{
 "_doc": "The Kraken (Pontoppidan, 1752-53): a sea-beast so vast that its back was taken for a cluster of small islands, its arms like the masts of ships, able to pull down the greatest ship. A giant squid come ashore: a long pointed mantle rising upright with fins at its tip, speckled and mottled; great glaring eyes and a hooked beak; thick arms spread over the ground, curling at their tips; and two long tentacles raised high, with broad clubbed ends lined with suckers. Built by tools/art/build_gears.py.",
